BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chansons of the Belle Époque Concert: Helen Lyons\, soprano & Ela
 ine Greenfield\, piano
DTSTART:20261115T160000
DTEND:20261115T170000
DTSTAMP:20261115T175202Z
UID:397fd530476cc9e1fac8926f9f5650@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Helen Lyons\, soprano\, and Elaine Greenfield\, piano\, will w
 hisk you away to the City of Light in a program of sumptuous music spannin
 g the period known as the Belle Époque. The second half of the 19th centu
 ry to the end of WWI was a time of great change\, not only politically\, b
 ut in the ever-shifting musical landscape. Experience music from the roman
 tic era’s decadent end through the height of Impressionism\, making char
 ming discoveries along the way. Music by Fauré\, Debussy\, Chausson\, Rav
 el and more.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Grace Congregational UCC\, 8 Court Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/chansons-o
 f-the-belle-epoque-concert-03-11-2026-10-47-14
END:VEVENT
