DESCRIPTION:It’s the VSO’s tenth season of Jukebox\, and we’re playi
 ng the hits! This series will feature wholly unique programs at our three 
 stops\, as we’ll be selecting pieces on the spot each evening. Drawing f
 rom music we’ve performed over nine years of concerts (while adding some
  new pieces to the roster)\, there will be 16 different possible selection
 s to choose from. You’ll hear heavy hitters of string quartet music like
  Beethoven and Bach\, modern compositions from Jessie Montgomery and Carol
 ine Shaw\, solos\, duos\, and music that spans the myriad different styles
  and genres you’ve come to expect from our Jukebox quartet. With the hel
 p of the audience\, the program will be decided by chance as eight pieces 
 are picked from our “jukebox” to perform. Every night will be one of a
  kind – it’s a game where we don’t know exactly what’s coming! Don
 ’t miss out as we celebrate ten years of this fun\, eclectic\, and intim
 ate concert series. Brooke Quiggins-Saulnier and Joana Genova\, violin\; S
 tefanie Taylor\, viola\; and John Dunlop\, cello. Hosted and curated by Ma
 tt LaRocca. The Paramount Theatre Pay-What-You-Can $15\, $20\, $25\, $30 +
  tax/fees The Paramount Theatre 30 Center St Rutland \, Vermont 05701 802-
 775-0903 boxoffice@paramountvt.org https://www.paramountvt.org/ Submit An 
 Event Find out what's happening in your neck of the woods with Vermont Pub
 lic's free Events newsletter. Email Address * Editorial Emails Breaking Ne
 ws | sent occasionally The Frequency | Daily News Update\, sent weekday mo
 rnings Capitol Recap | Vermont Legislature Wrap\, sent Fridays during the 
